<h2>The most compliance-intensive region we serve</h2>
<p>European markets apply the strictest residue and quality enforcement of any region we export to. EU maximum residue limits are tested actively at the border, and the UK — operating independently since Brexit — applies its own, separately maintained standards. Pre-shipment testing isn't optional here in any practical sense; it's the difference between a clean delivery and border rejection.</p>

<h2>Rotterdam as the entry point, not the destination</h2>
<p>A large share of goods clearing into "the Netherlands" in trade data are actually headed onward to Germany, France or elsewhere in the EU. If you're buying for delivery anywhere in Europe, importing via a Dutch distributor through Rotterdam is a common and often the most practical route, even when your own market isn't the Netherlands.</p>

<h2>EU and UK are two separate compliance tracks</h2>
<p>This is the point that trips up buyers moving between the two. TRACES registration and EU MRLs apply across EU member states; the UK's Food Standards Agency and Border Force run an independent system that started identical to the EU's at Brexit but can now diverge. Tell us specifically which you're shipping to.</p>
